From 4b26f11364cb32e6d2017c1934ba73fa5dd75341 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zack Maril <zmaril@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 17:50:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Add `-Zearly-metadata-verify`

Early metadata is only sound if two things hold, and this flag reports
when they don't, to stderr (build tools hide dependencies' diagnostics):

- No query that only full metadata can answer (optimized MIR, exported
  symbols, cross-crate inlinability, deduced parameter attributes, the
  panic strategy) is asked of a crate still loaded from early metadata.
  The answer would be wrong, and would stay cached after the swap to full
  metadata.
- Every definition left out of early metadata is nested in a body the
  interface doesn't depend on. If such a body was type-checked during the
  early write anyway, `interface_bodies` missed it.

The run-make test now passes it, and checks that it reports nothing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011C4oUhyTKGLkWYDeejZv2e
